---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Pool from "../components/Pool.astro";
const commands = {
  source: "git clone https://github.com/Ludion-ai/ludion.git\ncd ludion\nnpm ci\nnpm run build -w ludion-ai",
  scan: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js scan --dir /path/to/app",
  init: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js init --dir /path/to/app",
  patch: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js patch --dir /path/to/app",
  apply: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js patch --dir /path/to/app --apply",
  watch: "node packages/cli/dist/cli.js watch --dir /path/to/app --apply --interval 900",
};
const config = JSON.stringify({ schema: 1, dockerfile: "Dockerfile", test: ["php", "tests/smoke.php"], timeout_seconds: 120 }, null, 2);
---
<Base title="Try the PHP security preview | Ludion" description="Find and validate PHP Docker security updates. Run from source, choose your application test, then opt in to updating your Dockerfile.">
  <article class="start-page wrap">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <h1>Close your first patch gap.</h1>
      <p class="intro">Start with one PHP project. Check for a security update, validate it against your application, then choose whether to apply it.</p>
    </header>
    <Pool>
      <section class="sync" aria-labelledby="scan">
        <div class="install">
          <h2 id="scan">Check your PHP image</h2>
          <p class="where">Source preview · Node 24+ · Docker for validation. The published npm 0.1.4 release does not include these commands.</p>
          <p>After building this source revision, run:</p>
          <div class="command primary-command">
            <pre><code id="scan-command">{commands.scan}</code></pre>
            <button type="button" data-copy="scan-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy scan command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button>
          </div>
          <p class="wiring">Replace /path/to/app with your project directory. The scan reads its Dockerfile and checks PHP's official release metadata. It does not change your project.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="path" aria-labelledby="update-path">
          <h3 id="update-path" class="visually-hidden">The update path</h3>
          <ol class="flow">
            <li><span class="step-title">Detect</span><span class="step-detail">Official PHP security releases</span></li>
            <li><span class="step-title">Validate</span><span class="step-detail">Your application test, old and new</span></li>
            <li><span class="step-title">Apply</span><span class="step-detail">A digest-pinned Dockerfile change</span></li>
          </ol>
        </aside>
      </section>
      <p class="coverage">Supported: one-stage Dockerfiles with an exact official PHP image, such as php:8.4.26-cli-alpine. Multi-stage builds, floating tags, Java and host-installed PHP need manual handling. Production is not automatically redeployed.</p>
      <section class="reference" aria-labelledby="setup-details">
        <h2 id="setup-details">From a check to an update</h2>
        <details open>
          <summary><span>1 · Build the source preview</span><span class="summary-note">Keep the existing npm install separate</span></summary>
          <div class="detail-body"><p>Use the security-preview source revision. These instructions become available on the default branch when its pull request is merged.</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="source-command">{commands.source}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="source-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy source setup" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>2 · Choose your application test</span><span class="summary-note">Required before validation</span></summary>
          <div class="detail-body"><p>Create the configuration in your application:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="init-command">{commands.init}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="init-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy init command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Edit ludion.security.json. The example test path is a placeholder: replace it with a real test that is copied into your application image and can run offline as a non-root user.</p><div class="command"><pre><code>{config}</code></pre></div><p>Docker builds also run offline. Dependencies must already be available in the base image or your source tree. Network installs, remote ADD and external build stages are not supported.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>3 · Validate, then apply</span><span class="summary-note">Source changes are opt-in</span></summary>
          <div class="detail-body"><p>Download, build and test both versions without changing the Dockerfile:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="patch-command">{commands.patch}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="patch-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy validation command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>To validate again and apply the replacement only on success:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="apply-command">{commands.apply}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="apply-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy apply command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Review the receipt in your project's .ludion/security/ directory. A failed baseline, failed candidate or changed source leaves the Dockerfile untouched. Deploy the updated application through your normal process.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>4 · Keep checking automatically</span><span class="summary-note">While the process is running</span></summary>
          <div class="detail-body"><p>Check every 900 seconds and apply validated Dockerfile updates:</p><div class="command"><pre><code id="watch-command">{commands.watch}</code></pre><button type="button" data-copy="watch-command" data-copied="Copied" data-selected="Selected" aria-label="Copy watch command" aria-live="polite" hidden>Copy</button></div><p>Keep this foreground process running. Stop with Ctrl+C. This installs no background service and does not deploy production. Errors are reported; an unavailable source is never treated as a successful check.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>What leaves your machine</span><span class="summary-note">Source, requests and limits</span></summary>
          <div class="detail-body privacy"><p>The security commands request release metadata from php.net and official images through Docker. Source is copied to a temporary local build context and sent to your configured Docker daemon; use a local daemon to keep it on your machine. No source is uploaded to Ludion and the security commands send no telemetry.</p><p>The snapshot excludes .env files, .git, .ludion, node_modules, .ssh and .aws; it is not a general secret scanner. The application test runs inside a container, without host environment variables. Receipts stay in the project. The website uses Google Analytics; the legacy sync API retains its existing request-counting behavior.</p></div>
        </details>
        <p class="privacy-summary">A passing application test is evidence for that test. No newer security release is not a guarantee of safety. This preview does not inventory live servers or certify end-of-life support.</p>
      </section>
    </Pool>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]").forEach((button) => {
    const code = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy!);
    if (!code) return;
    button.hidden = false;
    const label = button.textContent;
    let reset: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      clearTimeout(reset);
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent ?? "");
        button.textContent = button.dataset.copied ?? label;
      } catch {
        const range = document.createRange();
        range.selectNodeContents(code);
        const selection = window.getSelection();
        selection?.removeAllRanges();
        selection?.addRange(range);
        button.textContent = button.dataset.selected ?? label;
      }
      reset = setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = label; }, 2000);
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .start-page {
    max-width: calc(1040px + var(--gutter) * 2);
  }
  .page-intro {
    padding-block: 16px 64px;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-title, clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px));
    font-weight: 560;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    max-width: 35em;
    font-size: var(--font-body, 16px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sync {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 15rem;
    gap: 48px 80px;
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 560;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .where {
    margin: 12px 0 24px;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .command {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 16px;
  }
  .primary-command {
    padding: 22px;
  }
  pre {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  pre code {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .primary-command pre code {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  button {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    min-height: 40px;
    min-width: 48px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 4px 6px;
    margin: -2px -4px 0 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  button:hover {
    background: var(--paper-2);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  button[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .result {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .result code {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .wiring {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    max-width: 42em;
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .path {
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .flow {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .flow li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 36px 24px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .flow li:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-left-color: transparent;
  }
  .flow li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 5px;
    left: -4px;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--muted);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .step-title,
  .step-detail {
    display: block;
  }
  .step-title {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .step-detail {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .step-detail.file {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 12px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .coverage {
    margin: 36px 0 0;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .coverage a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 4px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .reference {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  .reference > h2 {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--font-small, 13px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  details:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  summary {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px 24px;
    padding: 22px 28px 22px 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  summary::after {
    content: "+";
    position: absolute;
    right: 1px;
    top: 20px;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  details[open] > summary::after {
    content: "−";
  }
  summary:hover > :first-child {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .summary-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .detail-body {
    max-width: 44rem;
    padding-bottom: 28px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .detail-body > p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .detail-body .command + .command-label {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .detail-body .command-label {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .detail-body .consent {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .privacy-summary {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .sync {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 36px;
    }
    .flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 20px;
    }
    .flow li {
      padding: 18px 0 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .flow li::before {
      top: -4px;
      left: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .page-intro {
      padding-block: 8px 40px;
    }
    .sync {
      padding-top: 32px;
    }
    .primary-command {
      padding: 16px;
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .primary-command pre code {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .flow {
      grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);
      gap:0;
    }
    .flow li {
      padding:0 0 24px 20px;
      border-top:0;
      border-left:1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .flow li:last-child {padding-bottom:0;}
    .flow li::before {top:5px;left:-4px;}
    .step-title {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .step-detail {
      font-size: 12px;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .step-detail.file {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .reference {
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
    .summary-note {
      display: none;
    }
    .command {
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 14px;
    }
    .command pre code {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
